Hi All

Some key notes on this new grant programme which opened this week, as cover=
ed in today's briefing. For any client considering applying they should wat=
ch the recorded briefing (once available), as there are a lot of specific d=
etails and rules/requirements to take note of.

=C2=A312m total funding available
18-30 month projects
Grant size =C2=A3500k-=C2=A31m
Closing date 28.10.2026 11am
Project start 1.2.2027 and must close by 31.7.2029
10 scored questions, each with 400 word count limit
Must collaborate and must be business-led
Must include an SME
Must explain the opportunity for the materials innovation to be applied and=
 also describe any foreseen barriers to adoption
Must show the route to scale and how it will support UK advanced manufactur=
ing
Must include at least 1 named end user (who is operating within one of the =
8 IS sectors) -- note, this end user can be a funded or non-funded collabor=
ator, could be and end user on the project advisory board. RTOs and academi=
cs / academic organisations are not permitted. Government departments or re=
gulators could only be considered as an end user with adequate justificatio=
n.
Strict requirements to demonstrate having an end user - must have a clear, =
defined role within the project governance or work plan (so, for instance, =
having only 'letters of support' etc from an end user are not sufficient)

Focus areas: must fit one of these 4 themes and at least one of the associa=
ted sub-themes within each:

- Future healthcare -- Biocompatible and Regenerative Materials / Bioelectr=
onic Materials
- Structural material innovation - Sustainability / Surface Engineering / D=
esign and Deployment / Extreme Environments
- Power electronics and Connectivity - Wide and Ultra Wide Bandgap Material=
s / Advanced Connectivity Materials
- Metamaterials and Metasurfaces - Future Telecommunications and Advanced C=
onnectivity / Convergent Electronic-Photonic Technologies / Thermal, Acoust=
ic and Mechanical Metamaterials / Energy Security and Net Zero / Healthcare

Support available

Drop in clinic 1: 11/9/2026 10.30am-12 noon
Drop in clinic 2: 7/10/2026 10.30-12 noon
Finding a collaborator https://B2match.com/e/nmip26-crd
Light touch review by IUKBC -- https://iuk-business-connect.org.uk/ (at lea=
st 2 weeks before closing date)

Competition details here
https://apply-for-innovation-funding.service.gov.uk/competition/2569/overvi=
ew/a3448c9e-38ae-4759-957c-bccf6c40c281

Kind Regards,

